==Old English==

===Etymology===
From {{inh|ang|gem-pro|*strēlaz}}, {{m|gem-pro|*strēlō||arrow, ray, beam}}, from {{etyl|ine-pro|ang}} {{m|ine-pro|*strēl-}} {{m|ine-pro|*strēlā-||arrow, beam}}. Cognate with Old Saxon ''strāla'', Middle Dutch ''strael'' (Dutch [[straal]]), Old High German ''strāla'' (German [[Strahl]]). The Indo-European root was also the source of Old Slavic ''strěla'' (Russian {{l|ru|стрела}}).

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|/ˈstræːl/|lang=ang}}

